% Case searches (docs/user/reference/language.md §17.11), on a small rent
% support scheme.
%
% "which cases make it the case that <goal>" lists every case in which the
% goal holds: what a scenario would have to say (and not say) for it to hold,
% in general terms, with the scenarios of this program that meet each case.
% A case no scenario meets is a case the program's tests never tried; its
% answer comes with a ready-made scenario that meets it.
%
% "is there a case in which <goal>" looks for one case that breaks a
% property. Here the property is that nobody is both eligible for rent
% support and excluded from it. The scheme breaks it: a resident with an
% income between 15000 and 20000 who has no other benefits is eligible (the
% income limit is 20000) and excluded (the exclusion starts at 15000). The
% answer is that case, with an income chosen inside the gap.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a person* is eligible for rent support.
    *a person* is excluded from rent support.
    *a person* gets rent support.
    *a person* is a resident.
    *a person* has an income of *an amount*.
    *a person* receives other benefits.
    *a person* is a student.

the knowledge base case search includes:

a person gets rent support
    if the person is eligible for rent support
    and it is not the case that
        the person is excluded from rent support.

a person is eligible for rent support
    if the person is a resident
    and the person has an income of an amount
    and the amount < 20000
    and it is not the case that
        the person receives other benefits.

a person is excluded from rent support
    if the person is a student.

a person is excluded from rent support
    if the person has an income of an amount
    and the amount > 15000.

scenario ana is:
    ana is a resident.
    ana has an income of 12000.
    support expects answers ["ana gets rent support"].
    support for a student expects answers ["there is no such case: the search covered every case"].

scenario ben is:
    ben is a resident.
    ben has an income of 12000.
    ben is a student.
    support expects answers [].

scenario cara is:
    cara is a resident.
    cara has an income of 9000.
    cara receives other benefits.
    support expects answers [].

query support is:
    which person gets rent support.

query support cases is:
    which cases make it the case that
        a person gets rent support.

query both eligible and excluded is:
    is there a case in which
        a person is eligible for rent support
        and the person is excluded from rent support.

% A property that holds: nobody gets rent support as a student. The answer
% says that there is no such case, and that the search covered every case.
query support for a student is:
    is there a case in which
        a person gets rent support
        and the person is a student.
